 From: Wuzzy <almikes@aol.com>
To: lojban@googlegroups.com=20
Sent: Wednesday, December 4, 2013 7:50 AM
Subject: Re: [lojban] Alice essay
=20

I don=92t know how to write an essay but I am halfway through reading the
text in Lojban.

From what I can say so far is that the text has many, many mistakes. I
have made a personal list of this while reading the text; At some
point, I think, I just gave up counting.

Here is a summary of what I=92ve found so far:
- A few simple spelling mistakes.
- =93sai=94 is used in awkward places sometimes, like after a =93na=94. It
=A0 parses, but the meaning is undefined according to CLL
- the strange construction =93po'onai=94 is used somewhere, its meaning is
=A0 undefined AFAIK
- The ungrammatical construction =93ka'enai=94 is used several times
- There are multiple cases of sumti raising:
=A0 =A0 =93oiro=92a oiro=92a mi lerci=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 x1 is for an event, not a rabbit
=A0 =A0 =93ko ko ciksi=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 x2 does not allow a person
=A0 =A0 =93ei mi mi kajde lo=92e since (=85)=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 x1 and x3 are for events, not for persons or animals
=A0 =A0 =93oi ko mi na fanza=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 x1 expects an event, not a person
=A0 =A0 =A0 Suggestion: =93oi ko fi mi na fazgau=94
=A0 =A0 =93le reda fenki=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 Not sure, probably =93two crazy ones=94 are meant, but =93fenki=
=94 is for
=A0 =A0 =A0 crazy events, not for crazy persons
=A0 =A0 =93i la alis nasai jinvi le du=92u la=92e di=92u cu je=92urja=92o=
=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 x1 should be an agent. You also see the awkward =93nasai=94
=A0 =A0 =A0 construction in action here.
- It seems the word =93da=94 was sometimes intended to be used over a
=A0 sentence=92s border, which is not directly allowed in Lojban
- the quotation marks for the songs in chapter xa are missing
- =93krefu=94 is written =93KREFU=94 (in all-caps) on two occasions. Lojban
=A0 does not allow writing like that
- a LOT of lujvo (see appendix) were coined, many of them do not have
=A0 dictionary entries yet and are not declared nonce words with =93za'e=94=
.
=A0 Sorry, this is NOT the sane way to introduce lujvo into the language.
=A0 Lujvo are intended to have a fixed definition as contrast to tanru.
=A0 But a lujvo is pointless if it isn=92t defined; you could as well have
=A0 used a tanru. Things become complicated if someone not knowing about
=A0 the alis text writes a definition for one of these lujvo; it may or
=A0 may not be in the sense of the text. Sadly, that may already have
=A0 happened for some lujvo. This problem has a quick fix: Add =93za'e=94 i=
n
=A0 front of all lujvo in question. If that seems awkward to you, fall
=A0 back to tanru. And no, I am not talking about obvious lujvo with SE,
=A0 NAhE, NA, etc.
- I found 3 undefined fu'ivla so far. The same problems as for undefined
=A0 lujvo apply.
- For some reason, the text uses =93=92=94 instead ob =93'=94. The CLL says=
 =93'=94
=A0 is used and never uses =93=92=94.

Additionally, some experimental words are used: I noticed =93gumri=94 and
=93mu'ei=94 so far. You may think about experimental words what you want,
but you can=92t truthfully call your text to be in Lojban if you use any,
but rather in a dialect of Lojban (maybe call it =93experimental
Lojban=94?).


So long,
Wuzzy.

